WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.540
Степен сайта Коди Рашенхам, и then lock the everyday words that let you talk about rooms, furniture, and family life.

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:13.480
I'm Olya, and this is Privet Русский, Episode 64. The word of the day is Dome, Dome.

00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:24.000
It sounds like Dome, and rhymes with home. This word means house or home. Think of it as the Dome that shelters your whole family, your own little kingdom.

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:28.820
Мой Dome большой, my house is big, repeat after me, Dome.

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:32.320
Now that you know Dome, let's add more words about the ham.

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:38.400
The first one is комната, комната, it sounds like комната, and means room.

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:42.360
Remember, большая, from a few lessons ago, it means big.

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:47.140
And you can say, моя большая комната, next comes кухня, кухня.

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:50.180
It sounds like кухня, and means kitchen.

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:53.500
Imagine, кухня, where the cooking magic happens.

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:57.920
Мама готовит на кухне, корму шоу и мот кук в кухне.

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:00.720
Let's keep going with окно, окно.

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:03.900
It sounds like ok, no, and means window.

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:09.180
It comes from Ok or I, because a window is like the eye of the house.

00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:12.340
Я смотру в окно, I look out the window.

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:16.580
Now say, дверь, дверь, it sounds like дверь, and means door.

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:20.760
дверь sounds like deer, the door you open for dear friends.

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:23.800
Открой дверь, пожалуйста, open the door, please.

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:26.060
We are building a full picture now.

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:28.160
Next is стол, стол.

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:30.960
It sounds like стол, and means table.

00:01:31.580 --> 00:01:33.980
Мой ядим за столом, we eat at the table.

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:38.340
Then comes stool, stool, it sounds like stool, and means chair.

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:42.520
Stool is almost the same in English, so it is easy to remember.

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:45.220
Сидите на стуле, сид on the chair.

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:47.920
Ту more words finish our home picture.

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:52.440
Кровать, кровать, it sounds like crow, what, and means bed.

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:56.100
Picture crawling into your cozy crib, what at night?

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:59.060
Я сплю в кровати, I sleep in the bed.

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:04.740
Finally, lampa, lampa, it sounds like lampa and means lamp.

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:08.220
Лампа светит ярко, the lamp shines brightly.

00:02:08.980 --> 00:02:12.600
In Russian we use the word will to say something is in a place.

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:15.240
В комнате means in the room.

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:19.800
На кухне means in the kitchen, and the ending changes for this world.

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:24.720
In English stays the same, but Russian adds a special ending to show the place.

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:28.680
Now you can say where things are, like в комнате or на кухне.

00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:32.760
That small change makes your sentences sound natural right away.

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:37.240
In many Russian homes, the kitchen is the true heart of family life.

00:02:37.660 --> 00:02:41.620
People gather there for tea and long talks, more than in the living room.

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:44.620
Guests often step straight into the kitchen.

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:48.400
This shows that warned matters more than fancy furniture.

00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:50.940
Do you remember what комната means?

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:52.400
It means room.

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:59.780
Try using комнате three times today, for kids draw your dream Russian hum and label three rooms with the new words.

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:04.560
For adults, walk through your own hum and name each room out loud in Russian.

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:09.080
Something really cool about one of today's words is the story of окно.

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:16.740
It began long ago as око, the old word for I, because light enters the house just like light enters an I.

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:21.160
English window came from a different idea about wind and I.

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:27.880
The everyday Russian word for I is now glass, so око feels like a poetic memory from the past.

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:33.080
Picture the window as the house's watchful eye that stays open to the world.

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:35.720
Молодец, that means well done.

00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:41.500
Remember, every expert started as a beginner practicing today's words out loud,

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:44.700
even just once, and you'll be amazed how fast you learn.

00:03:45.020 --> 00:03:45.900
See you next time.

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:46.340
Пока!

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:47.920
That's Russian for buy.

